nevada has reached a settlement with the  advertising company mckinsey and company  for its advertising role in the ongoing  opioid crisis here in nevada  state attorney general aaron ford  explained in a press conference today  that he and his office wanted to hold  mckinsey accountable for its consulting  services  to big pharma companies particularly  they're advising on how to maximize  profits and target doctors to get them  to prescribe  more opioids a.g ford says the impact  opioids have on our state  is huge the devastation caused by the  opioid epidemic is felt by every mother  and father who has lost a child  it's felt by siblings who have lost a  sister or a brother  it's felt by friends and colleagues who  lost one of their own and obviously it's  felt by those still suffering from an  opioid addiction  with those effects in mind a.g ford  chose to pursue  separate legal action against the  company as he felt  our state deserve more than what we  would have received in a multi-state  settlement so from that nevada received  45 million dollars  a.g ford says he's proud that mckenzie  stepped forward to cooperate  and says that holding companies  responsible is the first step  in combating this ongoing crisis
 

